From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: App blocker on Android's Restricted background mode

Mobile Manager > App blocker: one switch per launcher app. On sets the
app to Android's Restricted background mode (the RUN_ANY_IN_BACKGROUND
app op ignored, exactly what Battery > Background use > Restricted sets
and reads) and stops the app now; Off allows background use again. The
platform holds the state, so Settings keeps no list of its own and the
battery page, Mobile Manager and the App Control Center always agree.
The apps the phone needs (home, dialer, SMS, keyboard, Settings) are
never listed. A blocked app can still be opened by hand; Freezer is the
way to stop that. The page warns that notifications, sync and sign-in
can stop.

Pure AppBlockerPolicy with host tests in tests/sable-apps.

---
